From: PS4 Linux Baikal Port <noreply@ps4-linux>
Subject: [PATCH] pci/msi/irqdomain: PS4 vendor quirks (Linux 6.15)

Adds PS4 vendor IDs to pci_ids.h plus probe/MSI-allocation adjustments
needed by the southbridge MFD glue. In 6.x the MSI subsystem was
restructured: arch/x86/kernel/apic/msi.c was replaced by io_apic.c +
vector.c + drivers/pci/msi/irqdomain.c + kernel/irq/irqdomain.c, and
include/linux/msi.h gained a new structure layout. This patch covers
all of that.

Sources:
  - crashniels/linux, ps4-linux-6.15.y-baikal at b3b6b1e4f
  - rmuxnet/ps4-linux-12xx commit 19ec7f4d1d9af199ec93ad6be8e635b38f735b86
    https://github.com/rmuxnet/ps4-linux-12xx/commit/19ec7f4d1d9af199ec93ad6be8e635b38f735b86

The Linux 6.18 port keeps only behavior still required by the PS4
southbridge drivers. It deliberately retains upstream's
DOMAIN_BUS_ANY guard; rmux restored that guard, so the older inverse
change is obsolete.

